  "question": {
    "text": "The integral value of <math><mi>a</mi></math>, for which the quadratic expression <math><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math> is negative for exactly two integral values of <math><mi>x,</mi></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "1",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let,&nbsp;<math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math> and <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />Since, the quadratic expression is negative for exactly two integral values<br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/e4afca79-1cee-4160-b404-6b944fdb9326.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:1.82014in;height:1.37986in\" /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>2</mn></math> and <math><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Hence, the integral value of <math><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
